# What the loop stores is a parameter of a block in which two ways meet. The look in front of the loop knew operators and written numbers for numbers, and no parameter: the store was passed over, the list that is stored into
# was not asked, and the loop was not built for lists of numbers at all. A parameter in which numbers alone meet is a number; so is what an edge narrows of a number, and a number with its sign changed.
# RUN(FLOOR): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# FLOOR: PutDoubleIndex
# RUN(SIZE): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# SIZE: PutDoubleIndex
# RUN(THERE): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# THERE: PutDoubleIndex
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
